  "description": "I’ve long held a huge affection for the Tracker bikes that ruled the roost in post war Britain, with their huge handlebars, kinked top tubes and dirt action attitude. This is my great ‘what if?’. What if the Trackers hadn’t died their natural death in the 1970s and continued to develop into mountain crushing quiver killers?\n\nThe finished article is the real deal – as shreddy and offroad capable as all my other frames, as bikepacking and touring capable as the Scrambler, but all wrapped up in a 29+ assisted ode to a glorious, forgotten past.",
